# Root .dockerignore — applies to every `docker build` in this repo
# regardless of which app's Dockerfile is used (apps/api, apps/web,
# apps/admin), since the build context is always the monorepo root.
#
# The concrete bug this exists to prevent: without it, `COPY packages
# ./packages` / `COPY apps/<app> ./apps/<app>` pulls in whatever
# `node_modules` already exists on the HOST (present on every real dev
# machine after `pnpm install`, absent only in a clean CI checkout) —
# including its pnpm symlinks, which on this platform point at absolute
# host paths (`C:/Code/lulwah/node_modules/...`). Copied into a Linux
# container, that overwrites the correct relative symlinks the image's
# own `deps` stage just installed with dangling ones, so a later `pnpm
# run build` step fails with "Cannot find module .../typescript/bin/tsc"
# despite the file being present moments earlier — this exact failure is
# how the gap was found, build-testing apps/api/Dockerfile locally rather
# than only in a clean CI runner, which never had a host node_modules to
# leak in the first place.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Build outputs — each Dockerfile builds these itself; a stale host copy
# should never leak into or shadow a fresh in-image build.
dist/
**/dist/
.next/
**/.next/
.turbo/
out/
**/out/

.git/
.claude/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/

*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
